:\"Willow Run Bomber Plant Tour\",\"matches\":false},{\"text\":\"Historic Ford-built B24 bomber plant, originally 1 mile long, running east-west\",\"matches\":false},{\"text\":\"Building passed through three owners: US Government, Kaiser Fraser, General Motors\",\"matches\":false},{\"text\":\"Built on a 1,500-acre Ford farm; Ford orchards extended to the west tree line\",\"matches\":false},{\"text\":\"All visible concrete is original; other areas heavily modified over the decades\",\"matches\":false},{\"text\":\"Workers paid in cash (many lacked bank accounts); vault door still on site in the GM annex\",\"matches\":false},{\"text\":\"Wartime Production Layout\",\"matches\":false},{\"text\":\"Chain drag rails ran through the building, pulling planes through in sections\",\"matches\":false},{\"text\":\"Multiple paint bays and metal prep bays in sequence, not one continuous conveyor\",\"matches\":false},{\"text\":\"Distance from current balcony to the tree line equals the length of a B24\",\"matches\":false},{\"text\":\"Turntables (four) positioned outside the building to shuffle finished planes sideways\",\"matches\":false},{\"text\":\"Norden bomb sites stored in a concrete room under the balcony for protection\",\"matches\":false},{\"text\":\"Not every plane received one: some used radio triggers or missions didn’t require it\",\"matches\":false},{\"text\":\"Burroughs factory (Hagerty and Plymouth Road) manufactured the Norden sites, continuing production into the Vietnam era\",\"matches\":false},{\"text\":\"Underground infrastructure: steam tunnels, electrical rooms, substations\",\"matches\":false},{\"text\":\"GM removed substations in the 1980s due to PCBs; new electrical system moved to balconies\",\"matches\":false},{\"text\":\"Aircraft on Site\",\"matches\":false},{\"text\":\"EC121 Warning Star (“Willie Victor 2”): radar plane with spinning bottom dish and hand-turned top dish\",\"matches\":false},{\"text\":\"Original equipment intact; crew bunks, galley, head,